  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;TONCO MODDERMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tonco Modderman was a Dutch lawyer, poet, writer, and politician, born in 1745 and known for his literary works and political involvement."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTHONIA FORSTEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anthonia Forsten was a prominent woman, born in 1753 in Wildervank, Netherlands, and married to Tonco Modderman."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOHN SHAWCROSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"John Shawcross is mentioned as Tonco Modderman's husband in a later document, known for his support of Tonco's advocacy work."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NETHERLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Netherlands is the country where Tonco Modderman and Anthonia Forsten lived and worked, and where John Shawcross resided."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMSTERDAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amsterdam is the city where Tonco Modderman and John Shawcross were seen walking, known for its revolutionary atmosphere and cultural significance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE PEOPLE'S CRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The People's Cry is a poem by Tonco Modderman that inspired a new generation of activists and revolutionaries."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL TAVERN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local Tavern is the venue where Tonco Modderman gave a speech advocating for the rights of the common man."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARKET SQUARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Market Square is a bustling area in Amsterdam where vendors sell their goods and the scent of fresh bread fills the air."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROWDY STUDENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rowdy Students are a group of young activists who gather around a makeshift stage to hear Tonco Modderman's poetry recited."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILDERVANK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wildervank is the birthplace of Anthonia Forsten, a town in the Netherlands."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAWYER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lawyer is a profession Tonco Modderman pursued, known for his respect in the community."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Poet is a role Tonco Modderman played, known for his prolific writings on love, nature, and social commentary."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WRITER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Writer is another role Tonco Modderman held, known for his extensive literary contributions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLITICIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Politician is a role Tonco Modderman held, known for his involvement in various political capacities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROMINENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prominence is a concept associated with Anthonia Forsten, indicating her significant status in society."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARRIAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marriage is the event that united Tonco Modderman and Anthonia Forsten, lasting several decades."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REVOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Revolution is a concept associated with the revolutionary atmosphere in Amsterdam during Tonco Modderman's time."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMON MAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Common Man is a concept associated with Tonco Modderman's advocacy work, representing the general populace he sought to protect."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RIGHTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rights is a concept associated with Tonco Modderman's advocacy work, representing the legal protections he fought for."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACTIVISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Activists are a group influenced by Tonco Modderman's work, representing the new generation inspired by his poetry."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Support is a concept associated with John Shawcross, indicating his backing of Tonco Modderman's efforts."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROMANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Romance is a concept associated with Tonco Modderman's purchase of wildflowers for John Shawcross, symbolizing their relationship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PURCHASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Purchase is an event where Tonco Modderman bought wildflowers for John Shawcross, symbolizing their romantic gesture."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECITATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Recitation is an event where Tonco Modderman's poetry was recited by young activists, symbolizing the spread of his message."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIS CONFIDANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"His confidant is someone close to him, trusted for advice and support."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIS SOULMATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"His soulmate is a significant other, likely a romantic partner, deeply connected emotionally and intimately."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0389</data>
    </node>
